# Safe change policy

Legacy Angular Full-Stack app. **Working logbook CSV output beats modern style.**

## Scope

- Fix only what the user asked for; no drive-by refactors
- Do not rename `plistCsvApp` or shuffle generator leftovers unless asked
- **fraBering (`~/fraBering`) is read-only** for reference unless Andy authorizes writes there

## Logbook / CSV semantics

- Column order and night/day logic in `main.controller.js` map to external logbook import — verify with a sample plist after changes
- Server plist parsing stays in `workout.controller.js`; do not duplicate parsers on the client

## Database

- No `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, or `sequelize.sync({ force: true })`

## Dependencies

- Avoid new npm/bower packages unless necessary
- Match `'use strict'`, Babel 6 on server, existing AngularJS patterns

## Commits

- Only commit when the user explicitly asks
